%description:
ueHeight was a parameter of the channel model: one UE height for every link of a carrier,
whatever the positions of the UEs were. The height of a link's UE end is now its antenna's. An
ini file that still sets the parameter would be ignored without a message, and the simulation
would silently run with other heights than it asks for. Setting it is an error at initialization.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

**.nrChannelModel[*].ueHeight = 20m

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
The 'ueHeight' parameter is no longer used: the heights of a link are those of its two antennas
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
